I'll read the spine contract first, then the full bundle, and answer only under the DOM/CSS3D feasibility lens.{"lens":"Implementation feasibility in DOM and CSS3D","object_model":"One chase of real DOM tiles under CSS3DRenderer: rectangular focusable nodes whose seating, misalignment, scale, and fall are transform-only. Profiled sockets/pegs and the hard shadow are decorative layers registered to those nodes, never mesh geometry or WebGL shading on the tiles.","states":["loose-compose","locking-in-order","seated-solid","hazard-ajar","pieing","bound-reflexive","no-bottom-held"],"mapping":[{"concept":"Photogram","verdict":"separate-surface","how":"One hard silhouette is not box-shadow. Precompute transitive-closure outline into a single canvas or SVG plane under the CSS3D scene; reproject every camera move from the same Three matrix so it stays registered. Umbra split at `|` is path math, not lighting. Feasible at ~5–15KB code, zero WebGL on tiles; registration drift under tilt is the real failure mode. Not a tile state."},{"concept":"Falls Through","verdict":"separate-surface","how":"Twelve columns on a plate is a second stage, not a chase mode. Spotless fall-through is a scripted translateZ/Y off the plate (no physics). Stain/tip on three dead protocols is opacity + rotate. Do not fold into lock-up without a scene switch; DOM node count and camera framing diverge from the stick."},{"concept":"Weight","verdict":"state","how":"Static per-tile `transform: scale(0.7–2.1)` from law in-degree, applied once at compose. Text stays vector-crisp if you scale the node (not a bitmap); non-integer scales can soft-blur on some GPUs—prefer whole-node scale over font-size reflow. Accessible name and focus stay on the same DOM node; hit target and focus ring scale with it. Do not animate weight during lock-up."},{"concept":"The Descent","verdict":"camera","how":"Animate CSS3DRenderer camera (or parent Object3D) down depth strata; pause per protocol element in causal order. Hairline laws = thin SVG/DOM strokes between tiles, not geometry. Unchosen `|` stubs are short strokes that simply stop—no branching physics. Cheap, no extra payload, reduced-motion = jump cuts to same stops."},{"concept":"Protocol Workbench","verdict":"gesture","how":"Compose is the workbench: drag elements onto the stick, empty sockets appear as labelled placeholders, hazards arm as the permanent 3.5° ajar joint. Full freeform bench UI is the same gesture vocabulary, not a second app—if product wants a separate bench chrome, that is polish on this gesture, not a new object."},{"concept":"Constraint Crystal","verdict":"camera","how":"Topological rank vs recorded S0–S4 is a camera/layout mode: re-stack or ghost-offset tiles where ranks disagree. No crystal mesh. Disagreement markers = hairlines or labels already legal in the document. Do not ship a second lattice object."},{"concept":"Substitution Space","verdict":"cut","how":"A lattice of alternate slabs multiplies full protocol tile sets. Under CSS3D each tile is a live DOM node with a nine-field name; N alternatives × M tiles blows layout, focus order, and payload headroom. Hazard punch-outs are already the ajar joint + pie hole. Show substitutes as family-keyed peg swaps on one stick, not a space of slabs."},{"concept":"The Denominator","verdict":"cut","how":"Nineteen-socket plate with dissolving no-bottom bars duplicates No Bottom Face and Photogram’s substrate story. Second plate = second surface, second focus graph. Encode survivor-unknown as empty sockets on the chase / pie hole shape, not a parallel monument."},{"concept":"The Needle","verdict":"cut","how":"Edge-notched card sort is a different input model (needle through deck). Emulate the outcome with family peg filters on the stick (show/hide by peg key); do not build a deck+needle widget. Gesture collision with compose/drag is high."},{"concept":"Valence (profiled edges, sockets, keyed pegs)","verdict":"state","how":"Not mesh pegs. Per tile: keep rectangular hit/focus box; draw profile with CSS `clip-path` on a decorative face OR one SVG path overlay (~1 extra node per tile if SVG). Family peg = shared path id so substitutes interchange. Seating is transform contact animation in dependency order, not collision. clip-path risks clipping text—prefer SVG edge under/over the text box. Cost: +0–1 node/tile, no layout reflow if absolute in the CSS3D object."},{"concept":"No Bottom Face","verdict":"state","how":"Async-impossible tile: on release without continuous lock-around, scripted fall through the stick (translate + opacity). No physics body. State `no-bottom-held` while pointer/focus keeps it in the continuous gesture."},{"concept":"Pie / physics fall","verdict":"state","how":"Scripted fall only: staggered transform keyframes (rotate + translateY + small random) out of the missing-law socket hole. A real 3D engine (cannon/ammo/rapier) is ~50–200KB and consumes most of the ~99KB gzip headroom for little gain. 2D matter.js still costs tens of KB and fights CSS3D. Ship tweened pie; abandon rigid-body stacking."},{"concept":"Strain deformation (2–4px, 4° open, 14Hz shiver, shear)","verdict":"state","how":"4° joint open and shear = CSS `rotate` / `skew` on the joint tiles—cheap, transform compositor. 2–4px ‘deformation’ = subpixel translate jitter, not mesh morph; true DOM mesh flex is fantasy. 14Hz shiver = rAF or stepped class toggles on a few hazard tiles only; do not shiver the whole forme or you jank. Reduced-motion: static 3.5° ajar, no shiver."}],"gestures":[{"input":"Drag element onto composing stick (pointer or keyboard move)","does":"Places tile in causal slot; shows empty required sockets; arms hazard ajar if co-presence illegal"},{"input":"Commit lock-up","does":"Quoins animate ~480ms; gaps close in dependency order via transforms until pegs/sockets meet or stick ajar"},{"input":"Lift / orbit (drag-tilt when solid)","does":"Chase rotates ~30°; solid = all children share one rigid parent transform; pie = unsupported tiles run scripted fall"},{"input":"Hold no-bottom tile through lock","does":"Continuous gesture keeps async-impossible element seated; release early → falls through"},{"input":"Drag while bound (reflexive)","does":"Pointer motion shears overconstrained joints; user force is the destroyer—no free rigid drag"},{"input":"Filter by family peg (needle substitute)","does":"Show only interchangeable peg keys; no separate needle UI"},{"input":"Descent scrub / step","does":"Camera stops per depth element; law hairlines draw; stubs stop short"}],"strain":"Valence-as-true-keyed-contact is the forced concept: DOM cannot socket-fit geometry, so profiles are cosmetics and seating is a lie told with transforms. Cost is either text-clipping clip-path, +1 SVG node per tile, or under-sold silhouettes. Photogram’s under-plane reproject is the second force—works until tilt/lift desyncs shadow from tiles. Most likely abandoned halfway: Photogram registration under live camera (or full physics pie if someone insists on an engine).","dissent_rulings":{"reflexive_death":"bind","dimming":"cut","why":"Bind is transform-constraint vs pointer—implementable without new payload; dimming is free CSS but fights focus order and the no-shadow/hazard-only colour rules, and reduced-motion already needs equal non-faded structure."},"build_order":["CSS3D stick + existing DOM tiles, shared rigid parent, keyboard focus intact (~0KB)","Dependency-order gap-close lock animation (transforms only, ~480ms)","Lift to 30° + drag-tilt when solid vs scripted pie fall when incomplete (~1–2KB tweens)","Weight: static scale 0.7–2.1× from in-degree; verify crisp text + a11y names","Hazard permanent 3.5° ajar + optional 14Hz shiver on hazard pairs only","Valence SVG/clip-path profiles + family peg ids (decorative; no physics)","No-bottom continuous-hold + fall-through","Bind gesture for reflexive death","Descent camera + law hairlines/stubs","Photogram under-plane silhouette if registration proves stable (else cut)","Falls Through as separate plate scene last","Never: Substitution Space lattice, Denominator plate, Needle deck, physics engine"],"what_others_will_force":"True interlocking peg/socket geometry or WebGL/mesh deformation on the tiles—both violate real-DOM CSS3D and will burn the 99KB headroom on engines and still fail focus/crisp text."}
